## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of advanced CSS layout concepts (container queries, grid masonry concepts, and motion accessibility) without JS.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid with grid-column: span and grid-auto-flow: dense
- Container Queries to adapt column count by parent size
- CSS Custom Properties for density toggling
- Accessible motion: respects prefers-reduced-motion

## Code Example
```css
:root{--gap:16px;--pad:12px;--font:14px;}
.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:var(--gap);}
.grid > .card{grid-column:span var(--span,1);opacity:0;transform:translateY(8px);animation:enter 0.4s var(--d,0s) both;}
@container (min-width:60em){.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);} .density-compact{--gap:8px;--pad:8px;--font:12px;}}
@container (max-width: 40em){.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(1,1fr);}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){.grid > .card{animation:none;}}
@keyframes enter{to{opacity:1;transform:none;}}
```

